I built and saved the workflow for slot w4-B. It passes lint with no errors, the situations check reports no problems, and a one-turn chat test starts correctly. The agent opened with "I am a digital assistant calling from Freya Bank, and the bank records this call. Am I speaking with Ms Lee?"

- **How I built it:** I didn't write it from scratch. I re-ran two generator scripts already in `out/` under this slot's name (`w4-B.gen.py`, then `w4-B.gen3.py`). These were left from earlier runs, so their exact origin isn't confirmed. They follow the calc file: its code step is the start node and leads into the opening, the account hook is set on `get_account`, and the router hands off to six specialist nodes (refused, hardship, dispute, already paid, restructuring, human).
- **One fix:** the situations check said the hardship node lacked the promise tool. I added `create_promise` there. It records only a date or amount the customer names themselves, after a read-back and a clear yes. If a result has `offer_instead`, it offers exactly that value.
- **Saves:** while fixing that, a quoting error made me save an incomplete version (version 23). Version 24 replaced it a moment later and is the current one.
- **Not done:** I skipped the rule-by-rule re-read of the brief (step 7) because of the time limit. I only spot-checked that the negotiate node has DATE FACTS, `offer_instead`, the per-product deadline rule and the date-of-birth format rule. No practice cases were run, as instructed.
- **Brief vs. extracted situations:** the `already_paid` first line says "close as `paid`", but under Brief B that applies only when every product is noted paid. The node's prompt already says this.

